  </data>
  <data name="AboutActive.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Active means recent input while tracking. It is an interaction-time proxy, not a measure of output.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AboutMissing.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unexplained gaps stay unrecorded, not inactive. Rankings compare active percentages of recorded awake time; card details show the evidence.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AboutPeriods.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hour and stretch cards use the selected day. Weekday patterns use the 28 days ending on that date. Partial recordings can influence comparisons.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AboutTime.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Times are local; timestamps are stored as UTC. App switches and sampling gaps up to 3 seconds can belong to one stretch, but observed inactivity breaks an active stretch.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AboutPrivacy.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Data stays on this PC. No window titles, URLs, keystrokes, screenshots or clipboard contents are recorded.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AboutSystemTime.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Locked, sleeping and confirmed powered-off periods count as inactive in totals and charts. Sleep and powered-off time are excluded from activity percentages and hour/weekday rankings. Power history uses Windows events; absent or ambiguous events remain unknown.</value>
  </data>
